  "id": "COMPOUND:31405 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Alstoyunine H is implicated in the target pathway leading to DNA polymerase iota through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that Alstoyunine H acts as a target for Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid and by another compound, (1R,2S,6R,7R,10S,11R,12R,14S)-10,11-dihydroxy-2,6-dimethyl-12-propan-2-yl-13-oxatetracyclo[8.5.0.02,7.012,14]pentadecane-6-carboxylic acid. Both of these compounds are known to target DNA polymerase iota. While the exact mechanism by which Alstoyunine H influences Caspase-5 is not fully elucidated, the shared pathway to DNA polymerase iota suggests a potential mechanism involving the modulation of caspase activity, which could in turn affect DNA polymerase iota function. The evidence supports a relationship where Alstoyunine H indirectly influences DNA polymerase iota through Caspase-5, though the precise nature of this interaction remains to be determined.",
